# 013 — dotted from-entry (`from gears import engine`, use site
# `engine.torque` in main.py): the PATH-SHAPED symbol wins over any hint
# (the python provider does not apply the 011-02 alias rewrite), so the
# provider looks for a TOP-LEVEL module `engine` — which does not exist.
# Offline mode (no network in the gate) refuses the fetch-on-demand and
# bails byte-for-byte. 011-08 review P1: the scope hint IS present (the
# app would send ["gears","engine","torque"] — original import path,
# item included) and the provider ignores it; with an EMPTY scope this
# probe could not demonstrate hint-ignoring, and the documented fix
# (scope_qualified_alias, cf. js_provider.rs) returns None unconditionally
# on an empty scope — it would land silently. With the hint present the
# current bail is unchanged (traced), and the fix flips this golden to a
# RESOLVED landing (project/gears/engine.py:11) — a conscious diff.
symbol=engine.torque
from_file=main.py
scope=["gears","engine","torque"]
root=project
kind=bail
bail=module `engine` not found and offline mode refuses to pip install
